<div class="faq-container">

<details>
<summary>
How can I choose among the best property dealers in India?
</summary>

<p>
Evaluate a dealer's business credentials, local market
knowledge, project information, transparency and communication.
Request written details of the property, understand applicable
fees and independently verify land ownership and permissions.
No single real estate provider is automatically suitable
for every buyer or location.
</p>
</details>

<details>
<summary>
What should I check before buying plots in Dholera?
</summary>

<p>
Verify the plot's location, survey number, title history,
land-use classification, relevant approvals, road access,
infrastructure status and total purchase price.
The broader development of Dholera does not automatically
confirm that an individual plot has all required permissions.
</p>
</details>

<details>
<summary>
Is it possible to explore farmhouse plots for sale in Pangot?
</summary>

<p>
Buyers can enquire about available land opportunities in
the Pangot region. However, Uttarakhand has specific
land-purchase and land-use restrictions, and eligibility
may vary by buyer and property. Verify applicable laws
and permissions with qualified local professionals.
</p>
</details>

<details>
<summary>
What should buyers know about commercial land near Dholera Airport?
</summary>

<p>
Airport proximity should be assessed alongside permitted
land use, physical access, ownership records, surrounding
infrastructure and development status. A nearby location
does not automatically mean a plot can be used commercially.
</p>
</details>

<details>
<summary>
Why is the ABCD Building area relevant to Dholera property searches?
</summary>

<p>
The ABCD Building is associated with the Dholera
Special Investment Region's administration and
development planning. Buyers exploring surrounding
plots should verify actual location and distances,
rather than relying on approximate marketing descriptions.
</p>
</details>

<details>
<summary>
What makes Pangot and Dholera different property markets?
</summary>

<p>
Dholera is associated with planned industrial
and urban development in Gujarat, while Pangot
is a hill-region location in Uttarakhand.
Their geography, land regulations, infrastructure
conditions and ownership considerations are different.
Buyers should evaluate each location independently.
</p>
</details>

